{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"design-grammar-process-and-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Design grammar process and controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Analytical state v1; exploratory mode. See "},{"type":"link","href":"model.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"model.md"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"evidence.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"evidence.md"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"reconstruction-and-compression-controls","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Reconstruction and compression controls"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"RC1 Reconstruct current Date control: P1(Date), each supplied carrier P2, E1 tag\nmapping P3, E2 queries P4, direct core/node SQLite P5, passing control P6.\nRC2 Reconstruct current Temporal failure: P1(Instant/PlainDate), E1 enumerable\nobject mapping yields {}, so R1 fails. SQL/residual and identity sort remain\nP4 observations; grammar records failure rather than inventing preservation.\nRC3 Reconstruct current #2002 receipt law: P5 wrapper plus E7 FIFO/publication\nlaw constrains R7 independently of any P3 format. No source transition is\nreimplemented in this grammar.\nRC4 Reconstruct index and cap paths: E4 shared SQL shape/upgrade plus E5 IN and\nwhole-statement cap, with P4 operations and P5 scoped-driver capability.\nAll four source arrangements are representable. This is an analytical\nreconstruction, not an executed implementation refinement proof."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ablation record:\nP1→cannot distinguish type erasure/spoofing; P2→loses metadata-only/literal\ncarrier reach; P3→cannot express old bytes or query representation; P4→cannot\ndistinguish persisted value from meaningful filter/order; P5→incorrectly borrows\nwrapper/host evidence; P6→green but unreached or correlated judgment admitted.\nR1→{} accepted; R2→top-level-only fix admitted; R3→canonical-string order conflated\nwith semantic order; R4→false-negative prefilter admitted; R5→IN/cursor/index\ntranslation can diverge; R6→invalid overwritten action disappears; R7→durable\nrollback falsely claimed as public rollback; R8→direct-core results lend wire\nsupport; R9→old index/reader mismatch hidden; R10→competing scheduler/model owner.\nO1 removal erases same-order/different-equality distinctions; O2 literal/index\nencoding diverges; O3 failure scope conflates durable and public state; O4\nconstructor registration substitutes for transport; O5 index presence substitutes\nfor matching SQL. Each relation is retained for that distinguishing loss.\nDemoted candidates: provider brand/version is a boundary annotation, not a\nprimitive; retry/generation machinery is excluded because no new lifecycle is\nneeded to express the repair; generic custom codecs are outside this extraction."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model-checking status: not applicable to this static compatibility grammar.\nNo new concurrency/state-transition model is asserted. Existing stateful\ncontracts are imported constraints whose tests remain with their primary\nowners. No TLC run or proof of their integration is claimed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Range status: UNTESTED. No independently held-out marginal source was supplied.\nAll dates/calendars/precision cases used here are construction or future test\nobligations, not independent range evidence.\nNegative control: a plain object with Symbol.toStringTag='Temporal.Instant'\nand a toString method is not thereby an admitted native Temporal value. R1\nrequires real brand validation. Another exclusion: assigning lexical order to\na Temporal kind with no DB-defined ordering is not generated by R3."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"process-freeze-and-projection-support","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Process freeze and projection support"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Analytical state v1 freezes E1–E10, I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10, O1–O5, RC1–RC4,\nU1–U4 and F1–F3 before a human brief or stress readings are drafted.\nProjection claims must map to these IDs: type preservation→I1/R1/R2;\nquery triangle→I3/I4/R3–R5/O1/O2; oracle ownership→I5–I8/R6–R10;\nlimits→U1–U4/range/distortion. Later stress readings may expose conditions but\nmust not silently rewrite this frozen grammar or count as held-out range tests."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The source reconstruction used one read-only subagent for existing oracle\nownership. The primary agent owned extraction, reconstruction, compression,\nand the fracture/tension scans. A separate fresh subagent received only C1\nand its source basis for the hostile assay; it could not see F1–F3 or the other\nstress readings. No new Field Log or broader workflow was started."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Post-freeze probes belong to the fracture scan; they are not held-out grammar\nrange evidence. Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, temporal-polyfill 0.3.0 produced:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\"instant\":{\"a\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"b\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000000001Z\",\"semanticCompare\":-1,\"sqliteLexicalEarlier\":0},\"plainDate\":{\"a\":\"2026-01-02\",\"b\":\"2026-01-02[u-ca=japanese]\",\"semanticCompare\":0,\"sameKindAndText\":false}}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"No source compiler or serializer was changed for these probes. They constrain\nplausible implementations without claiming any candidate is implemented."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"post-freeze-hostile-reading-and-projection-audit","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Post-freeze hostile reading and projection audit"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fresh hostile auditor completed its reading against C1 at e21c280f3 without\nsibling forms or the fracture/tension readings. The primary agent checked the\ncited mechanisms and saved all five attacks as HA1–HA5 in\n"},{"type":"link","href":"hostile.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"hostile.md"}]},{"type":"text","value":", including their repair conditions and dispositions.\nNo material attack was dropped and no finding was ranked. The agent's probe\nresults are attributed observations; its source-derived failure scenes were not\nexecuted against a candidate patch."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Two qualifications matter when reading the frozen layers:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"E8's separately callable SingleProcessCoordinator method projects wire values,\nbut ordinary wrapper routing bypasses the remote-demand queue for that\ncoordinator ("},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"persisted.ts:3238"},{"type":"text","value":"). Neither source fact proves every public\nsingle-process query rejects Temporal. HA5 retains a non-single-process\nreceiving witness as open."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I4/R4's matching-row containment does not by itself establish preservation of\nrejection outcomes. HA3 records this additional observation-contract question;\nit does not silently strengthen the frozen rule or invent a guarantee that\nevery Boolean branch must execute. HA4 similarly treats format reversibility\nas unresolved rather than attributing that promise to C1."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The README projects the frozen grammar, then separately reports the requested\nstress readings. These readings are addenda, not independent grammar range tests\nand not a revised grammar version. A future revised grammar must explicitly\ncarry any adopted condition into a new version."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Consequential README claim"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exact support"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Current revision, #2002 and repeated RED result"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Evidence preamble; E7/E10; current-main replay receipt"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Value preservation crosses serializer/query/public boundaries"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"P1–P5; O1–O5; E1–E4/E8"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Six constrained case dimensions and example"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Case/Environment/HistoryWitness definitions; P1–P6; RC1/RC2"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Supported kinds/carriers/brands and unchanged plain data"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I1/I2; R1/R2; E1/E9"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Storage/equality/order and SQL/index distinctions"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I3/I4/I7; R3–R5/R9; O1/O2/O5; E2–E5; U1"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Durable rejection, superseded actions, wrapper receipts/FIFO, caps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I5–I7; R6/R7/R10; E5–E7; RC3/RC4"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime/route qualifications and old-byte information limit"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I8/I9; R8/R9; U2–U4; E8–E10"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Existing owners, no replacement lifecycle and receiving limits"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"I10/R10; E6/E7/E10; primary ownership table"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Unranked adjacent forms and losses"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F1–F3; U1–U4; dynamics/constraints/boundaries"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hostile findings and evidence limits"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"HA1–HA5 and concrete scene in hostile.md; qualifications above"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Conditional marker fracture and executed scalar probes"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"FRA1–FRA3, controls and distortion in fracture.md; probe receipt above"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Three unranked tensions and rejected publication framing"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"T1–T7, retained A–C, provenance and controls in tensions.md"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Provisional status, range, exclusions and decomposition losses"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Model preamble/distortion; range and model-check statuses; negative control; U1–U4"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Layer reconstruction audit: the primary brief preserves each consequence that\nchanges the result: type preservation, existing-data compatibility, distinct\nquery relations, durable/public checkpoints, binding/driver constraints,\nboundary-qualified support, owner reuse, unranked alternatives and unresolved\nmechanisms. The linked Model retains I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10 and O1–O5; Evidence\nretains source authority and owner limits; Process retains RC1–RC4 and all\nablations, range/model-check exclusions and this support map. The three stress\nrecords preserve failure constructions, controls, weakening evidence and\ninduced distortions. No confidence, recommendation, priority or support claim\nwas added by compression. User selection among the provisional tensions is\nstill pending; it is not inferred from silence."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"design-grammar-process-and-controls","text":"Design grammar process and controls","level":1},{"id":"reconstruction-and-compression-controls","text":"Reconstruction and compression controls","level":2},{"id":"process-freeze-and-projection-support","text":"Process freeze and projection support","level":2},{"id":"post-freeze-hostile-reading-and-projection-audit","text":"Post-freeze hostile reading and projection audit","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# Design grammar process and controls\n\nAnalytical state v1; exploratory mode. See [model.md](model.md) and [evidence.md](evidence.md).\n\n## Reconstruction and compression controls\n\nRC1 Reconstruct current Date control: P1(Date), each supplied carrier P2, E1 tag\nmapping P3, E2 queries P4, direct core/node SQLite P5, passing control P6.\nRC2 Reconstruct current Temporal failure: P1(Instant/PlainDate), E1 enumerable\nobject mapping yields {}, so R1 fails. SQL/residual and identity sort remain\nP4 observations; grammar records failure rather than inventing preservation.\nRC3 Reconstruct current #2002 receipt law: P5 wrapper plus E7 FIFO/publication\nlaw constrains R7 independently of any P3 format. No source transition is\nreimplemented in this grammar.\nRC4 Reconstruct index and cap paths: E4 shared SQL shape/upgrade plus E5 IN and\nwhole-statement cap, with P4 operations and P5 scoped-driver capability.\nAll four source arrangements are representable. This is an analytical\nreconstruction, not an executed implementation refinement proof.\n\nAblation record:\nP1→cannot distinguish type erasure/spoofing; P2→loses metadata-only/literal\ncarrier reach; P3→cannot express old bytes or query representation; P4→cannot\ndistinguish persisted value from meaningful filter/order; P5→incorrectly borrows\nwrapper/host evidence; P6→green but unreached or correlated judgment admitted.\nR1→{} accepted; R2→top-level-only fix admitted; R3→canonical-string order conflated\nwith semantic order; R4→false-negative prefilter admitted; R5→IN/cursor/index\ntranslation can diverge; R6→invalid overwritten action disappears; R7→durable\nrollback falsely claimed as public rollback; R8→direct-core results lend wire\nsupport; R9→old index/reader mismatch hidden; R10→competing scheduler/model owner.\nO1 removal erases same-order/different-equality distinctions; O2 literal/index\nencoding diverges; O3 failure scope conflates durable and public state; O4\nconstructor registration substitutes for transport; O5 index presence substitutes\nfor matching SQL. Each relation is retained for that distinguishing loss.\nDemoted candidates: provider brand/version is a boundary annotation, not a\nprimitive; retry/generation machinery is excluded because no new lifecycle is\nneeded to express the repair; generic custom codecs are outside this extraction.\n\nModel-checking status: not applicable to this static compatibility grammar.\nNo new concurrency/state-transition model is asserted. Existing stateful\ncontracts are imported constraints whose tests remain with their primary\nowners. No TLC run or proof of their integration is claimed.\n\nRange status: UNTESTED. No independently held-out marginal source was supplied.\nAll dates/calendars/precision cases used here are construction or future test\nobligations, not independent range evidence.\nNegative control: a plain object with Symbol.toStringTag='Temporal.Instant'\nand a toString method is not thereby an admitted native Temporal value. R1\nrequires real brand validation. Another exclusion: assigning lexical order to\na Temporal kind with no DB-defined ordering is not generated by R3.\n\n## Process freeze and projection support\n\nAnalytical state v1 freezes E1–E10, I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10, O1–O5, RC1–RC4,\nU1–U4 and F1–F3 before a human brief or stress readings are drafted.\nProjection claims must map to these IDs: type preservation→I1/R1/R2;\nquery triangle→I3/I4/R3–R5/O1/O2; oracle ownership→I5–I8/R6–R10;\nlimits→U1–U4/range/distortion. Later stress readings may expose conditions but\nmust not silently rewrite this frozen grammar or count as held-out range tests.\n\n\nThe source reconstruction used one read-only subagent for existing oracle\nownership. The primary agent owned extraction, reconstruction, compression,\nand the fracture/tension scans. A separate fresh subagent received only C1\nand its source basis for the hostile assay; it could not see F1–F3 or the other\nstress readings. No new Field Log or broader workflow was started.\n\nPost-freeze probes belong to the fracture scan; they are not held-out grammar\nrange evidence. Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, temporal-polyfill 0.3.0 produced:\n\n```json\n{\"instant\":{\"a\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"b\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000000001Z\",\"semanticCompare\":-1,\"sqliteLexicalEarlier\":0},\"plainDate\":{\"a\":\"2026-01-02\",\"b\":\"2026-01-02[u-ca=japanese]\",\"semanticCompare\":0,\"sameKindAndText\":false}}\n```\n\nNo source compiler or serializer was changed for these probes. They constrain\nplausible implementations without claiming any candidate is implemented.\n\n## Post-freeze hostile reading and projection audit\n\nThe fresh hostile auditor completed its reading against C1 at e21c280f3 without\nsibling forms or the fracture/tension readings. The primary agent checked the\ncited mechanisms and saved all five attacks as HA1–HA5 in\n[hostile.md](hostile.md), including their repair conditions and dispositions.\nNo material attack was dropped and no finding was ranked. The agent's probe\nresults are attributed observations; its source-derived failure scenes were not\nexecuted against a candidate patch.\n\nTwo qualifications matter when reading the frozen layers:\n\n- E8's separately callable SingleProcessCoordinator method projects wire values,\n  but ordinary wrapper routing bypasses the remote-demand queue for that\n  coordinator (`persisted.ts:3238`). Neither source fact proves every public\n  single-process query rejects Temporal. HA5 retains a non-single-process\n  receiving witness as open.\n- I4/R4's matching-row containment does not by itself establish preservation of\n  rejection outcomes. HA3 records this additional observation-contract question;\n  it does not silently strengthen the frozen rule or invent a guarantee that\n  every Boolean branch must execute. HA4 similarly treats format reversibility\n  as unresolved rather than attributing that promise to C1.\n\nThe README projects the frozen grammar, then separately reports the requested\nstress readings. These readings are addenda, not independent grammar range tests\nand not a revised grammar version. A future revised grammar must explicitly\ncarry any adopted condition into a new version.\n\n| Consequential README claim | Exact support |\n| --- | --- |\n| Current revision, #2002 and repeated RED result | Evidence preamble; E7/E10; current-main replay receipt |\n| Value preservation crosses serializer/query/public boundaries | P1–P5; O1–O5; E1–E4/E8 |\n| Six constrained case dimensions and example | Case/Environment/HistoryWitness definitions; P1–P6; RC1/RC2 |\n| Supported kinds/carriers/brands and unchanged plain data | I1/I2; R1/R2; E1/E9 |\n| Storage/equality/order and SQL/index distinctions | I3/I4/I7; R3–R5/R9; O1/O2/O5; E2–E5; U1 |\n| Durable rejection, superseded actions, wrapper receipts/FIFO, caps | I5–I7; R6/R7/R10; E5–E7; RC3/RC4 |\n| Runtime/route qualifications and old-byte information limit | I8/I9; R8/R9; U2–U4; E8–E10 |\n| Existing owners, no replacement lifecycle and receiving limits | I10/R10; E6/E7/E10; primary ownership table |\n| Unranked adjacent forms and losses | F1–F3; U1–U4; dynamics/constraints/boundaries |\n| Hostile findings and evidence limits | HA1–HA5 and concrete scene in hostile.md; qualifications above |\n| Conditional marker fracture and executed scalar probes | FRA1–FRA3, controls and distortion in fracture.md; probe receipt above |\n| Three unranked tensions and rejected publication framing | T1–T7, retained A–C, provenance and controls in tensions.md |\n| Provisional status, range, exclusions and decomposition losses | Model preamble/distortion; range and model-check statuses; negative control; U1–U4 |\n\nLayer reconstruction audit: the primary brief preserves each consequence that\nchanges the result: type preservation, existing-data compatibility, distinct\nquery relations, durable/public checkpoints, binding/driver constraints,\nboundary-qualified support, owner reuse, unranked alternatives and unresolved\nmechanisms. The linked Model retains I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10 and O1–O5; Evidence\nretains source authority and owner limits; Process retains RC1–RC4 and all\nablations, range/model-check exclusions and this support map. The three stress\nrecords preserve failure constructions, controls, weakening evidence and\ninduced distortions. No confidence, recommendation, priority or support claim\nwas added by compression. User selection among the provisional tensions is\nstill pending; it is not inferred from silence.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# Design grammar process and controls\n\nAnalytical state v1; exploratory mode. See [model.md](model.md) and [evidence.md](evidence.md).\n\n## Reconstruction and compression controls\n\nRC1 Reconstruct current Date control: P1(Date), each supplied carrier P2, E1 tag\nmapping P3, E2 queries P4, direct core/node SQLite P5, passing control P6.\nRC2 Reconstruct current Temporal failure: P1(Instant/PlainDate), E1 enumerable\nobject mapping yields {}, so R1 fails. SQL/residual and identity sort remain\nP4 observations; grammar records failure rather than inventing preservation.\nRC3 Reconstruct current #2002 receipt law: P5 wrapper plus E7 FIFO/publication\nlaw constrains R7 independently of any P3 format. No source transition is\nreimplemented in this grammar.\nRC4 Reconstruct index and cap paths: E4 shared SQL shape/upgrade plus E5 IN and\nwhole-statement cap, with P4 operations and P5 scoped-driver capability.\nAll four source arrangements are representable. This is an analytical\nreconstruction, not an executed implementation refinement proof.\n\nAblation record:\nP1→cannot distinguish type erasure/spoofing; P2→loses metadata-only/literal\ncarrier reach; P3→cannot express old bytes or query representation; P4→cannot\ndistinguish persisted value from meaningful filter/order; P5→incorrectly borrows\nwrapper/host evidence; P6→green but unreached or correlated judgment admitted.\nR1→{} accepted; R2→top-level-only fix admitted; R3→canonical-string order conflated\nwith semantic order; R4→false-negative prefilter admitted; R5→IN/cursor/index\ntranslation can diverge; R6→invalid overwritten action disappears; R7→durable\nrollback falsely claimed as public rollback; R8→direct-core results lend wire\nsupport; R9→old index/reader mismatch hidden; R10→competing scheduler/model owner.\nO1 removal erases same-order/different-equality distinctions; O2 literal/index\nencoding diverges; O3 failure scope conflates durable and public state; O4\nconstructor registration substitutes for transport; O5 index presence substitutes\nfor matching SQL. Each relation is retained for that distinguishing loss.\nDemoted candidates: provider brand/version is a boundary annotation, not a\nprimitive; retry/generation machinery is excluded because no new lifecycle is\nneeded to express the repair; generic custom codecs are outside this extraction.\n\nModel-checking status: not applicable to this static compatibility grammar.\nNo new concurrency/state-transition model is asserted. Existing stateful\ncontracts are imported constraints whose tests remain with their primary\nowners. No TLC run or proof of their integration is claimed.\n\nRange status: UNTESTED. No independently held-out marginal source was supplied.\nAll dates/calendars/precision cases used here are construction or future test\nobligations, not independent range evidence.\nNegative control: a plain object with Symbol.toStringTag='Temporal.Instant'\nand a toString method is not thereby an admitted native Temporal value. R1\nrequires real brand validation. Another exclusion: assigning lexical order to\na Temporal kind with no DB-defined ordering is not generated by R3.\n\n## Process freeze and projection support\n\nAnalytical state v1 freezes E1–E10, I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10, O1–O5, RC1–RC4,\nU1–U4 and F1–F3 before a human brief or stress readings are drafted.\nProjection claims must map to these IDs: type preservation→I1/R1/R2;\nquery triangle→I3/I4/R3–R5/O1/O2; oracle ownership→I5–I8/R6–R10;\nlimits→U1–U4/range/distortion. Later stress readings may expose conditions but\nmust not silently rewrite this frozen grammar or count as held-out range tests.\n\n\nThe source reconstruction used one read-only subagent for existing oracle\nownership. The primary agent owned extraction, reconstruction, compression,\nand the fracture/tension scans. A separate fresh subagent received only C1\nand its source basis for the hostile assay; it could not see F1–F3 or the other\nstress readings. No new Field Log or broader workflow was started.\n\nPost-freeze probes belong to the fracture scan; they are not held-out grammar\nrange evidence. Node 24.19.0, SQLite 3.53.3, temporal-polyfill 0.3.0 produced:\n\n```json\n{\"instant\":{\"a\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00Z\",\"b\":\"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000000001Z\",\"semanticCompare\":-1,\"sqliteLexicalEarlier\":0},\"plainDate\":{\"a\":\"2026-01-02\",\"b\":\"2026-01-02[u-ca=japanese]\",\"semanticCompare\":0,\"sameKindAndText\":false}}\n```\n\nNo source compiler or serializer was changed for these probes. They constrain\nplausible implementations without claiming any candidate is implemented.\n\n## Post-freeze hostile reading and projection audit\n\nThe fresh hostile auditor completed its reading against C1 at e21c280f3 without\nsibling forms or the fracture/tension readings. The primary agent checked the\ncited mechanisms and saved all five attacks as HA1–HA5 in\n[hostile.md](hostile.md), including their repair conditions and dispositions.\nNo material attack was dropped and no finding was ranked. The agent's probe\nresults are attributed observations; its source-derived failure scenes were not\nexecuted against a candidate patch.\n\nTwo qualifications matter when reading the frozen layers:\n\n- E8's separately callable SingleProcessCoordinator method projects wire values,\n  but ordinary wrapper routing bypasses the remote-demand queue for that\n  coordinator (`persisted.ts:3238`). Neither source fact proves every public\n  single-process query rejects Temporal. HA5 retains a non-single-process\n  receiving witness as open.\n- I4/R4's matching-row containment does not by itself establish preservation of\n  rejection outcomes. HA3 records this additional observation-contract question;\n  it does not silently strengthen the frozen rule or invent a guarantee that\n  every Boolean branch must execute. HA4 similarly treats format reversibility\n  as unresolved rather than attributing that promise to C1.\n\nThe README projects the frozen grammar, then separately reports the requested\nstress readings. These readings are addenda, not independent grammar range tests\nand not a revised grammar version. A future revised grammar must explicitly\ncarry any adopted condition into a new version.\n\n| Consequential README claim | Exact support |\n| --- | --- |\n| Current revision, #2002 and repeated RED result | Evidence preamble; E7/E10; current-main replay receipt |\n| Value preservation crosses serializer/query/public boundaries | P1–P5; O1–O5; E1–E4/E8 |\n| Six constrained case dimensions and example | Case/Environment/HistoryWitness definitions; P1–P6; RC1/RC2 |\n| Supported kinds/carriers/brands and unchanged plain data | I1/I2; R1/R2; E1/E9 |\n| Storage/equality/order and SQL/index distinctions | I3/I4/I7; R3–R5/R9; O1/O2/O5; E2–E5; U1 |\n| Durable rejection, superseded actions, wrapper receipts/FIFO, caps | I5–I7; R6/R7/R10; E5–E7; RC3/RC4 |\n| Runtime/route qualifications and old-byte information limit | I8/I9; R8/R9; U2–U4; E8–E10 |\n| Existing owners, no replacement lifecycle and receiving limits | I10/R10; E6/E7/E10; primary ownership table |\n| Unranked adjacent forms and losses | F1–F3; U1–U4; dynamics/constraints/boundaries |\n| Hostile findings and evidence limits | HA1–HA5 and concrete scene in hostile.md; qualifications above |\n| Conditional marker fracture and executed scalar probes | FRA1–FRA3, controls and distortion in fracture.md; probe receipt above |\n| Three unranked tensions and rejected publication framing | T1–T7, retained A–C, provenance and controls in tensions.md |\n| Provisional status, range, exclusions and decomposition losses | Model preamble/distortion; range and model-check statuses; negative control; U1–U4 |\n\nLayer reconstruction audit: the primary brief preserves each consequence that\nchanges the result: type preservation, existing-data compatibility, distinct\nquery relations, durable/public checkpoints, binding/driver constraints,\nboundary-qualified support, owner reuse, unranked alternatives and unresolved\nmechanisms. The linked Model retains I1–I10, P1–P6, R1–R10 and O1–O5; Evidence\nretains source authority and owner limits; Process retains RC1–RC4 and all\nablations, range/model-check exclusions and this support map. The three stress\nrecords preserve failure constructions, controls, weakening evidence and\ninduced distortions. No confidence, recommendation, priority or support claim\nwas added by compression. User selection among the provisional tensions is\nstill pending; it is not inferred from silence.\n"}
